  "conclusion": "METAR observations are fundamentally hourly (one per station-hour). Only ~2-5% of hours have supplemental observations for sub-hourly resolution. ASOS 1-min data exists but provides reliable coverage only for KNYC. 3-min entry timing would NOT materially improve accuracy for the daily bucket prediction task. The value of higher-frequency timing would be in intraday trading (same-day entry/exit), which is a separate pipeline. For daily settlement prediction, hourly entry timing is sufficient."
